            <ArticleTitle>Spinal cord stimulation for refractory angina in a patient implanted with a cardioverter defibrillator.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>143-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spinal cord stimulation is currently used to treat refractory angina. Some concerns may arise about the possible interaction concerning the spinal cord stimulator in patients already implanted with a pacemaker or a cardioverter defibrillator. We are going to describe the successful implantation of a spinal cord stimulator in a patient previously implanted with a cardioverter defibrillator.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
